# Line endings.
#
# The sources are stored with LF (that is what git normalises to), but these
# files are RUN by cmd.exe on Windows: a .bat with LF endings breaks on labels,
# `goto` and multi-line blocks. Pin them so every checkout - Windows, Mac or a
# copy of the folder - gets the form that actually runs.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Already-compressed or opaque files: never touch their bytes.
*.xlsx binary
*.XLSX binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
